azgor schrieb:
> 
> [2]: Exercise charisma when you get intimate with foocubi --Chilliwack

You mean charisma should be made exercisable? Currently, In and Ch
can't be exercised _at all_.

> [3]: Eating the corpse of a spellcasting monster like a kobold shaman
> or a gnomish wizard should restore a small amount of energy.
> --NESoutlaw_

If it weren't too much, that might be nice and would again increase
the practical value of tinning kits.

> [4]: New conduct: Levitationless

Yet another uninteresting conduct. Hmph.

> [5]: If you perform an action that kills yourself directly while on an
> altar, you get 'Sacrified yourself to [God]' on your tombstone
> --Patashu

Sacrificing in NetHack requires #offering the corpse. Bit difficult,
ne?

> [6]: Crowning should be something benefitial if you can handle the
> prayer timeout. Something really nice, like full
> blessing/greasing/fooproofing/enchanting your inventory, or a handful
> of magic markers/blessed full healing/holy water. Or a grappling hook,
> dozen lumps of royal jelly and t-shirt :P --Patashu

Crowning gifts, you mean? 
The source fastest to hand suggests:
Potion of healing (full healing for dogs), a stack of arrows, a tame
dog, a potion of booze, 360 towels, a t-shirt, ten cheap plastic
imitations of the amulet of Yendor, a tame but permanently confused
raven (no hawks in NetHack), an ornamental cope, a long bow, 4 or 5
cursed (dirty) eucalyptus leaves, a horn of plenty which will only
ever produce adventure beast droppings, 144 lances, a historical
statue of a cow and a dunce cap.

> [7]: YAFM if you finish off a partly eaten food item someone started
> eating in a bones file. "Do you know where this has been?" --Patashu

Yuck. Yes, i'm all for it.

> [8]: <HairyDude> would be nice if you could see your message history
> just after dying --BenUrban

I'm afraid i don't see the point.

> [9]: Baby Silver Dragons should have reflection. --greqrg

Do other baby dragons have the properties/resistances of the
full-grown shape, too? If yes, giving baby silvers reflection would be
reasonable.

> [10]: Rogues should start with stethoscopes. --BenUrban
> 
> [11]: ...or maybe Rangers. --BenUrban

I don't see the rationale behind the suggestion.

> [12]: New conduct (already being done informally) - sightless.

Clear case of "not again" - this idea is far from new.

> [13]: Darts thrown at straw golems always disappear, because you'll
> never find a needle in a haystack. --DGMavn

Heh, appropriate and not unbalancing. Why not.

> [14]: Eating wands should have some effect, eg. eating a wand of death
> should kill you. --DGMavn

Perhaps treat eating a wand like breaking it? Sounds interesting, but
i think it might cause serious trouble - not because of the effects
when the player eats a wand (hardly ever happens anyway), but because
rust monsters, xorns and especially gelatinous cubes could evoke some
spectacular effects this way.

> [15]: Spell of Reduce Hunger - Converts your mana into nutrition.

No. Spells _cause_ hunger, unless you're playing a wizard with 18+ In;
and that's one of the balancing mechanisms for spellcasting. 

It would make foodless _way_ too easy for spellcasting types, too.

